{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the tav of תקדמנו precedes before the face of HaShem, and the verb takes two objects, namely the king, who is preceded by blessings." "<b>A crown</b> — gold with fine gold, precious stones around it, for so is the custom of kings. And it is possible that the tav of תקדמנו is feminine, on account of blessings, as in the manner of: בנות צעדה עלי שור (Judges 5:10)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The tav referenced is the prefix of תקדמנו (the verbal form in the verse), not the word כי; the syntax of Ibn Ezra's sentence is compressed.", 1 "He cites Judges 5:10 to show a feminine plural verb with no explicit subject, analogous to reading תקדמנו as feminine singular with 'blessings' as the implied subject."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:02.886570096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}